Upstream build identity: declared candidate baseline commit d743267388641bc76f17c45ce8b4c231aed1d32c.
The installation this copy was taken from carries no git metadata, so the commit is
not independently verifiable from it; what tools/verify-artifacts.mjs does check
locally is the installed package name/version, the per-file sha256 of every copy,
the exact recorded diff of every modified file, and one installation-wide build
identity (baseline.buildIdentity in provenance.json) computed over the packages
this replacement rides on. "Build identity" means: for every package in that list,
hash every file below it (recursively, skipping nested node_modules and symlinks),
sort by path, and hash the resulting path+content-hash lines. A version string
alone cannot tell two builds of the same version apart; the digest can.

Copied files (recorded hashes and the exact differing lines live in provenance.json, shipped in this package):
  lib/index.js         copy; the host entry adds the build-identity check
                       (see "Modification summary" below)
  lib/client.js        copy; the module registration id and the persistence
                       selection differ from upstream
  lib/types/**/*.d.ts  verbatim copies

Authored files (not copied from upstream; hashed in provenance.json):
  lib/baseline-identity.js
                       build identity algorithm and the runtime guard. It
                       recomputes the digest and refuses to serve the settings
                       provider when the running installation is not the recorded
                       build. The terminal preflight (tools/lib/preflight.mjs)
                       imports this same file, so the gate an operator runs and
                       the check the provider runs are one implementation.

Modification summary, host half (lib/index.js): apply() calls assertBaselineIdentity() from
lib/baseline-identity.js before it registers anything, so the provider refuses to serve when
the running installation is not the recorded build.

Modification summary, browser half (lib/client.js): the browser half no longer derives its persistence mode
from remote.$host.isLoopback. Upstream keeps every preference process-local
("memory") on a non-loopback page; this copy keeps the Host-backed persistence
("host") on every authenticated page. remote.$host.isLoopback itself, the
transport fence, the entry id ui-settings and the page plugins are unchanged.

The Host half additionally refuses to serve at all unless this installation is the
recorded build: lib/index.js imports lib/baseline-identity.js and checks the
package name, the version, the recorded file list and the digest before it
registers anything, and it throws instead of registering when they differ. There
is no environment variable, version range or compatibility exemption that bypasses
that check, so a mismatch is a refusal rather than a silently different behaviour.
Terminal recovery: node tools/overlay.mjs diagnose / rollback / record.
